homelab-keepalived (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: VRRP virtual-IP failover (keepalived) for the
    homelab-* internet-facing edge. Floats a public VIP between edge
    nodes via unicast VRRP on the internal plane; the VIP and a
    master-only default route move together on failover; optional
    per-service health tracking lowers priority so a healthy peer wins;
    ships a safe (no-flush, delete-by-comment) VRRP firewall drop-in for
    the drop-policy input AND output base chains.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Fri, 03 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500
